<task id="228" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>An open budget inquiry's To Do cannot be completed without a disposition, and recording one closes its Signal promptly (#1984, #1991 DI-101)</title>
    <phase>13 Deferred-issue triage group C (R1 close-out)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF code (.cs).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Adds an invariant check to a shared child-record write route (one server owner per invariant, ADR-002) and enqueues re-evaluation; a wrong check blocks every To Do completion.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>group-c-2026-11-26a</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>ChildRecordEndpoints To Do completion path, InquiryDispositionService and the Worklist inquiry notice; no overlap with 225/226/230.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, signals, frontend, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5-1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-26: "Yes, start group C" (deferred-issue triage group C, notes/deferred-triage-2026-11.md). Read gh issue view 1984 (with its uac-r2 comment) and gh issue view 1991, and DI-101 in notes/defer-issues.md. (1) #1984: PATCH /api/v1/child-records/sprk_todo/{id} with statecode=1 (Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs, the core MarkCompleteExecutor also calls) completes an inquiry-outcome To Do with no disposition; TodoDetail's Complete button uses it. Apply the worklist's check InquiryDispositionService.FindOpenInquiryOfTodoAsync (open + outbound only; a fault fails closed) on that route when it completes a sprk_todo, returning the same 409 inquiry.disposition_required; TodoDetail (src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/TodoDetail) shows plain words pointing to recording the outcome. (2) #1991: POST /api/v1/inquiries/{serviceRequestId}/disposition (InquiryDispositionService.RecordAsync) completes the To Do but leaves its open Do-lane Signal until the nightly run. Preferred fix from the issue: enqueue re-evaluation of that subject's open Signals through the existing evaluator event-hook IJobHandler path (D-12; grep the budget-revision hook), so it closes as ConditionCleared within seconds; then remove the stopgap notice (Worklist/inquiryDisposition.ts:50 and its test). Read docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md and .claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md first. Line numbers at origin/master d43fc9e16d.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer: .NET 10 BFF write paths and ADR-004 jobs, React/Fluent v9 shared components.</role>
  <goal>No path completes an open budget inquiry's outcome To Do without a disposition, and recording a disposition closes the To Do's Signal within the job latency instead of at the next nightly run.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>The route serves every child-record table and every To Do: the check must run only for sprk_todo completion and cost nothing for a To Do with no open inquiry beyond the existing lookup. A closed inquiry's To Do completes as today. The re-evaluation writes no human-resolution Decision Record (BR-1); its one Routine ConditionCleared record is the one the nightly would write (D-145b, idempotent key; corrected 2026-11-26 after the PR #3273 review). It must not stamp unchanged Signals (D-61). Run /conflict-check (ChildRecordEndpoints is shared).</background>
  </context>
